      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "**Godot version:**\r\n3.1.1 Headless\r\n\r\n**OS/device including version:**\r\nLinux, version shouldn't matter\r\n\r\n**Issue description:**\r\nGodot headless export path is confusing.\r\n\r\n**Steps to reproduce:**\r\n`./bin/Godot_v3.1.1-stable_linux_headless.64 -v \"./${projectDir}/project.godot\" --export HTML5 \"./${exportDir}/index.html\"`\r\n\r\nI expect this to export to export to the relative path of my current directory, `\"./${exportDir}/testProject.html\"`, but instead it tries to export to the relative path of the `project.godot` file, so `./${projectDir}/${exportDir}/testProject.html`\r\n\r\nThis can be bypassed with the absolute path `${realpath \"./${exportDir}/testProject.html\"}`, but it is not oblivious that is the problem from the error messages.\r\n\r\nThis is not technically a bug, but it is very confusing and can cause headless builds to fail and give no useful error message if you don't realize Godot is using the project file's relative path.",
